      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Audio to MIDI (MuScriptor)\n\nTurns a recording into a multi-instrument MIDI file: pitch, start, end and instrument for every note, drums included. Velocity is not transcribed, so every note comes out at the same loudness.\n\nNodes: [jtydhr88/ComfyUI-muscriptor](https://github.com/jtydhr88/ComfyUI-muscriptor), MIT. Model: [MuScriptor](https://github.com/muscriptor/muscriptor) by Kyutai and Mirelo. The code is MIT; the weights are CC BY-NC 4.0, non-commercial use only.\n\n```dotenv\nCOMFY_ASSET_PROFILES=muscriptor\n```\n\nThe profile puts `muscriptor-large.safetensors` (5.5 GB) in `ComfyUI/models/muscriptor/` and the sample song in `ComfyUI/input/`. The weights are gated: accept the licence on [MuScriptor/muscriptor-large](https://huggingface.co/MuScriptor/muscriptor-large) with the `HF_TOKEN` account. Approval is instant.\n\nThe MIDI file is written to `ComfyUI/output/midi/` and its path shows in the preview node. Open it in a DAW or in MuseScore.\n\n### Settings\n\n- `instruments`: leave empty and the model decides. A comma-separated list such as `acoustic_piano, drums` limits the output to those groups. Unambiguous short forms work (`timp,dist`). The tooltip lists all 35 names.\n- `beam_size` 2 or more switches to beam search: slower, sometimes more accurate.\n- `prelude_forcing` carries notes held across a 5-second chunk boundary into the next chunk. Leave it on. Turning it off allows `batch_size` above 1, which is faster but worse at the boundaries.\n- The loader also offers `small`, `medium` and `large`. Those download from Hugging Face into its cache on first use, which for `large` is a second copy of the file above. `small` and `medium` are faster and less accurate."
      ],
      "title": "Credit, model and settings",
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
